595	   Companion to the @theme tokens above. Only the two effects every one of the
596	   four approved mockups leans on as a *background/nav treatment* (not a
597	   one-off component style — those live as React components in
598	   components/portal-v2/primitives.tsx) get a reusable class here: the ambient
599	   drifting gradient-mesh page background, and the floating-glow active-nav
600	   pill. Everything else (cards, stat tiles, gauges) is a component, not a
601	   global class, because it needs props (tone, value) a CSS class can't take.
602	   Nothing in this block touches .card, .btn-*, .glass, or any selector an
603	   existing page depends on — it's purely new `.pv-*`-prefixed surface. */
604	@layer components {
605	  /* Base surface used by components/portal-v2/primitives.tsx's <Surface>.
606	     Kept here (rather than only inline in the component) so any hand-written
607	     markup that needs the exact same treatment before the component library
608	     covers it can apply one class instead of restating the shadow stack. */
609	  .pv-surface {
610	    @apply rounded-pv-lg border border-white/[0.07] bg-pv-surface-1;
611	    box-shadow: 0 1px 0 0 rgb(255 255 255 / 0.03) inset, 0 8px 32px -12px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.5);
612	  }
613	  /* "Raised" variant — the wizard's sticky order-summary rail and the
614	     billing cockpit header sit a hair above the base surface: a stronger
615	     border and an added soft brand-glow, not just a darker fill. */
616	  .pv-surface-elevated {
617	    @apply rounded-pv-lg border border-white/[0.14] bg-pv-surface-1;
618	    box-shadow:
619	      0 1px 0 0 rgb(255 255 255 / 0.04) inset,
620	      0 12px 36px -14px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.55),
621	      0 0 46px -22px rgb(111 71 245 / 0.35);
622	  }
623	
624	  /* Ambient slow-drifting gradient-mesh background (shell mockup's canvas
625	     hero, reimplemented as pure CSS so any page can opt in with one class
626	     instead of mounting a <canvas> + rAF loop). Apply to a `position:
